"zen.mock.meditation.title" = "A moment of stillness";
"zen.mock.meditation.opening" = "Welcome. Find a position where your body can rest. There is nothing you need to achieve here.";
"zen.mock.meditation.1" = "Notice the support beneath you. Let your shoulders soften. Allow the breath to come and go in its own way.";
"zen.mock.meditation.2" = "Feel the air at your nose. There is no need to change its rhythm. Simply notice it.";
"zen.mock.meditation.3" = "When a thought arrives, you can let it be there. Then gently return your attention to your body.";
"zen.mock.meditation.4" = "Rest for a while with what is already here. One breath. The weight of your body. The sounds around you.";
"zen.mock.meditation.closing" = "Feel the support beneath you again. Move your fingers whenever you are ready. Carry a little of this stillness into your next moment.";
"zen.mock.focus.rest" = "For now, let the tasks of the day wait. Notice where your body might soften just a little.";
"zen.mock.focus.stress" = "If things feel busy, you do not need to solve everything. Find a steady sensation in your body and rest your attention there.";
"zen.mock.focus.focus" = "We are practising returning to one thing at a time. Choose the breath as a gentle place for your attention.";
"zen.mock.focus.sleep" = "There is nothing else to finish now. You can rest and let the story drift past.";
"zen.mock.story.title" = "The garden at dusk";
"zen.mock.story.opening" = "At the end of a quiet path is a small garden. The day is slowly settling down. Behind a low wall stands a cherry tree, with a single paper lantern hanging from its branches. The light is warm and soft. You do not need to follow every word. It is all right simply to rest.";
"zen.mock.story.1" = "The gate is slightly open. Beyond it, a path of smooth stones winds through the moss. The stones still hold a little warmth from the day. Someone swept the path earlier this evening. Here and there a small leaf has landed since then, and no one has needed to move it. Everything can stay just as it is.";
"zen.mock.story.2" = "Further into the garden stands a bench of pale wood. Beside it is a cup that still carries the faint scent of tea. One last raindrop falls from the little house into a clay pot. Then it is quiet again. Only the leaves move, so slowly that the movement is almost invisible.";
"zen.mock.story.3" = "The lantern makes a soft circle on the gravel. At the edge of its light, a pair of sandals rests beside the steps. Nothing is waiting to be finished. Through an open window there is a folded blanket and a book set aside for the evening. The breeze passes gently through the room and out into the garden.";
"zen.mock.story.4" = "Above the wall, the sky fades from blue to silver. The little tree is completely still for a moment. Then one branch sways slowly back and forth. The scent of damp earth lingers in the air. There is no need to hurry the night along. It arrives in its own time, gentle and quiet.";
"zen.mock.story.closing" = "The light of the lantern grows softer. The path, the tree and the little bench rest in the dusk. There is nowhere to go and nothing to hold on to. The garden is still. Evening slowly becomes night.";

